        <mxCell id="pat-n6" value="&lt;span style='background-color:#8A6D00;color:#FFFFFF;font-size:8px;font-weight:bold;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;'&gt;&amp;nbsp;COMMENT&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Transactional Outbox&lt;/b&gt;: state, outbox row and event-log row commit atomically. Redis is only updated &lt;b&gt;after&lt;/b&gt; commit, so the duplicate can lag but never lead. The same Lua call appends to oversee:feed, so Oversee sees an event only once its state is in Redis. &lt;b&gt;Event Log&lt;/b&gt;: append-only history for replay and audit." style="shape=note;size=14;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=3;fillColor=#FFF9DB;strokeColor=#D6B656;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#1A1A1A;spacingRight=14;" vertex="1" parent="pat-F6">
