        <mxCell id="pat-n7" value="&lt;span style='background-color:#8A6D00;color:#FFFFFF;font-size:8px;font-weight:bold;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;'&gt;&amp;nbsp;COMMENT&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chain of Responsibility&lt;/b&gt;: a read tries Redis, then PostgreSQL; a PostgreSQL miss is authoritative, so the read chain ends at Tier 2. &lt;b&gt;Cache-aside / write-through&lt;/b&gt;: Redis is a deliberate, disposable duplicate of PostgreSQL. Every entity write is a version compare-and-set, so live writers and the healer can run together without regressing a key. &lt;b&gt;Memento&lt;/b&gt;: Tier 3 is never read live; it serves only an operator-run restore." style="shape=note;size=14;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=3;fillColor=#FFF9DB;strokeColor=#D6B656;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#1A1A1A;spacingRight=14;" vertex="1" parent="pat-F7">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="616" width="680" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
