        <mxCell id="pat-n9" value="&lt;span style='background-color:#8A6D00;color:#FFFFFF;font-size:8px;font-weight:bold;padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;'&gt;&amp;nbsp;COMMENT&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Observer of committed state&lt;/b&gt;: Oversee reads oversee:feed, which is appended in the same atomic Lua step that copies state into Redis, and wakes the &lt;b&gt;RiskSweep&lt;/b&gt;, which re-evaluates the account from one PostgreSQL snapshot (level-triggered, no timers). &lt;b&gt;Strategy&lt;/b&gt;: every risk rule is a plugin with one evaluate(); &lt;b&gt;Registry&lt;/b&gt; builds them from config, so adding a rule never changes Oversee. Levels are ordered; the most severe one wins." style="shape=note;size=14;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=3;fillColor=#FFF9DB;strokeColor=#D6B656;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#1A1A1A;spacingRight=14;" vertex="1" parent="pat-F9">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="816" width="680" height="80" as="geometry" />
