        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;AUTH_FAILED&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style='font-size:9px' color='#555555'&gt;credential error; page;&lt;br&gt;no retry loop&lt;/font&gt;" tooltip="Credential errors are not network errors: at most 3 attempts, then stop and page (critical). An operator fixes the credential. The state is recorded per adapter and credential generation (Secrets Manager version id or token_generation) in PostgreSQL, so a new leader does not retry until it changes, and it never triggers an abdication. It is left for AUTHENTICATING only when the credential generation changes, or an operator re-arms the adapter (authenticated, audited)." id="sm-a_af">
